Track 3: Maestro Calavera
- Story & Context: They say Maestro Calavera was not born but forged in the first full eclipse, his heart a drum, his voice the very creak of the carnival rides as the world briefly paused its spin, a spectral guide for those who dared to dance in the fleeting dark. The legend recounts how he once commanded the shadow itself to dance the Mambo with him, his skeletal mask reflecting the terrifying, beautiful corona of the hidden sun. "The sun will bleed, but I will dance, until its shadow frees me," echoed his guttural chant through the eclipse-chilled air, sealing his myth.
